  <iati-identifier>XM-DAC-7-PPR-250000413</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-7" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the Netherlands</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ex-ante evaluation of the effects of raising the treshhold criterium of to 50% for ngo&apos;s that want to receive funding from the new policy framework</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this evaluation is:
1) An ex-ante analysis of the possible effects of increasing the threshold criterion of non-BZ income from 25% to 50% for civil society organisations that wish to receive resources under thematic subsidy policy frameworks;
2) An ex-ante analysis of the possible effects of introducing a threshold criterion for civil society organisations that receive direct subsidies;
3) Practical recommendations and action perspectives regarding whether or not to increase the threshold criterion from 25% to 50% for organisations within thematic subsidy policy frameworks, with attention to the option of a phased introduction;
4) Practical recommendations and action perspectives regarding whether or not to introduce a threshold criterion for organisations that receive direct subsidies, including the possibility of a 50% threshold and the consideration of a phased approach.</narrative>
  </description>
